node_modules/
dist/

# Snapshot cache and volume history — regenerated from the feeds, not source.
.cache/

# Holds UPSTOX_ACCESS_TOKEN — credentials must never be committed.
# .env.example is the template.
.env
.env.local
# The office copy — a full set of live credentials, same rule as .env itself.
.env.office

# Timestamped copies made before editing .env. These are FULL COPIES of the real file,
# credentials and all, and one of them (.env.backup-20260808-213723) was committed and pushed
# to origin/master before this rule existed — see the note in .env.example. The pattern is
# here so the next backup cannot repeat it.
.env.backup-*

*.log

# Cached Upstox bars for the strategy research — 107MB of 1-minute data across 209 symbols plus
# the daily series. Regenerated by research/fetch-minutes.ts and research/fetch-daily.ts, so it is
# an artefact rather than source, and it is vendor market data that should not be redistributed
# through a repository. The SCRIPTS in research/ are source and are committed; only the pull is not.
research/data/

# The 15%/30% risk study — kept on the machine that ran it, not in the repository.
#
# An exception to the line above, and it is worth saying why rather than leaving the two rules
# looking like they contradict each other. The `study*.mjs` scripts are committed because they
# are how the shipped displacement rule was derived, and anyone reading that rule needs them.
# These seventeen are a one-off answer to a single question — whether a 15% stop and a 30% target
# can work on this strategy — and the answer (no: -2.9% of premium a trade, because the round
# trip plus a day of decay is already 8.5%) lives in the alert channel's own comments and in
# JOURNAL_TP_PCT / JOURNAL_SL_PCT. The scripts are the working, not the result.
research/risk-*.mjs
